while (condition) {
    code to be executed repeatedly as long as the condition is true
}

for (initialization; condition; increment) {
    code to be executed repeatedly as long as the condition is true
}

for (initialization, condition; increment) {
    code to be executed repeatedly as long as the condition is true
}

In the first case, the "code to be executed repeatedly as long as the condition is true" is executed the first time through the loop, and then repeatedly as long as the condition is true.  
In the second case, the "code to be executed repeatedly as long as the condition is true" is executed the first time through the loop, and then repeatedly as long as the condition is true.  In the third case, the initialization is executed once, the condition is tested once, and the increment is executed once.  This repeats as long as the condition is true.

